# Firebase Realtime Database Security Rules

This document explains the Firebase Realtime Database rules used by Smart Water Guardian. The rules are defined in `firebase.rules.json` at the repository root.

---

## Complete Rules File

```json
{
  "rules": {
    ".read": true,
    ".write": "auth != null",
    "users": {
      ".read": true,
      ".write": "auth != null",
      "$uid": {
        ".read": true,
        ".write": "auth != null"
      }
    },
    "alerts": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null"
    },
    "properties": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null"
    },
    "meters": {
      ".read": true,
      ".write": true
    },
    "thresholds": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null"
    },
    "messages": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null"
    },
    "reviews": {
      ".read": true,
      ".write": "auth != null"
    },
    "bills": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null"
    },
    "admin_settings": {
      ".read": "auth != null",
      ".write": "auth != null"
    }
  }
}
